    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July), making all three required changes.\n\n**`Owner.java`** (`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`):\n- Added a private `fiscalYearStart(LocalDate)` helper \u2014 the fiscal year's starting calendar year: July\u2013December belongs to the fiscal year starting that year; January\u2013June belongs to the one that started the previous year.\n- Added `getFiscalYear()` \u2192 returns `\"FY<YY>\"` (two digits of the fiscal-year start) derived from the already-business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`.\n- Changed `getMembershipNumber()`'s year segment from the raw registration-date year to the fiscal-year `YY`.\n- Changed the tenure rule in `getMembershipPoints()` from a `> 365`-day window to counting **elapsed fiscal years** (`fiscalYearStart(now) - fiscalYearStart(registrationDate) >= 1`), and removed the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** (drives the generated `OwnerDto` + the MapStruct mapping):\n- Added the read-only `fiscalYear` property (`FY<YY>`), so it serializes into the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response via the existing name-based MapStruct mapping \u2014 no mapper change needed.\n- Updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to document the fiscal-year basis.\n\n**Convention note:** I labelled the fiscal year by its *start* year, which keeps the existing `-M26` example and audit output consistent (a registration date of Oct 2026 \u2192 `FY26` / `-M26`). The acceptance test (`fiscalYear` matches `FY\\d{2}`) and the full suite pass.\n\nOne judgement call worth flagging: the spec said tenure must be \"counted in elapsed fiscal years\" without pinning an exact threshold, so I mapped the old \"more than 365 days\" (\u2248 crossed a year boundary) to \"one or more elapsed fiscal years.\" Happy to adjust the threshold if you intended a different cutoff.",
