    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe structure is clean and idiomatic for this file:\n\n- The `fiscalYearStart(LocalDate)` extraction is the right unit of shared logic. It centralizes the \"fiscal year starts 1 July\" rule in one private static helper and is reused by all three call sites (`getFiscalYear`, `getMembershipNumber`, `getMembershipPoints`), so the rule lives in exactly one place.\n- `getFiscalYear()` sits naturally among the other small `@Transient` derived getters (`getMembershipNumber`, `getCheckDigit`, `getMembershipPoints`), matching their one-liner style and Javadoc conventions.\n- The tenure change reads cleanly inline (`fiscalYearStart(now) - fiscalYearStart(registrationDate) >= 1`) and no longer needs the `ChronoUnit` import, which was correctly removed.\n- Javadoc and the OpenAPI schema were updated in lockstep with the behaviour, including cross-`@link`s between the new getter and the two dependents.\n\nThe only mild duplication is the `String.format(\"%02d\", fiscalYearStart(...) % 100)` idiom appearing in both `getFiscalYear` and `getMembershipNumber`. Since the membership number embeds the two digits in a different template (`-M<YY>` vs `FY<YY>`), it can't reuse `getFiscalYear()`'s string directly, and both already share the meaningful logic via `fiscalYearStart`. Extracting a further two-digit helper would be over-abstraction for a trivial format call, so leaving it as-is is the more natural choice here.",
